# kk: Add barrier variants that take visibility options
# https://gitlab.freedesktop.org/mesa/mesa/-/merge_requests/46468 state=closed
# ### What does this MR do and why?

<!--Describe in detail what your merge request does and why.-->

```
kk: Use device visibility at the end of render encoders

end_encoder ends every encoder with an ALL to ALL barrier with resource alias visibility. Render encoders that never enabled visibility results now use device visibility for that barrier. Render encoders that did, and compute encoders, keep resource alias visibility, because occlusion results are read back through another address of the same memory.

The ALL to ALL wait is unchanged on every encoder: pipeline barriers recorded outside an encoder and vkCmdWaitEvents2 emit nothing and rely on it.

Open question for review: KosmicKrisp places images in a heap that a buffer also maps. A test that renders into one placed texture and reads an aliased texture and the heap buffer in the next encoder showed no stale data with device visibility, but it also showed none with no visibility option at all, so it does not settle whether device visibility is enough for aliased memory.

The first commit adds barrier wrappers that take the visibility options (also part of !).

Testing (Apple M5 Pro, macOS 27.2): no dEQP-VK regressions against main on a 107,052 case list (synchronization, synchronization2, query pools, memory mapping, binding and barriers) or on a 79,312 case list; occlusion queries 441 cases × 80 with no failures.

Assisted-by: LLM
